# ways — a way's symbol stands on its line, and is one way from either end
#
# The plain way between two neighbours, a door, a stair, a path or a climb is not on a card: its
# symbol is on the line the map draws for it. One line is one symbol and one tree, so a click names
# exactly that way and the mind has nothing to choose among. What stands in areas nobody has been
# to is on their cards all the same, and answers no click until a known way leads there.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Yard" --period dawn --organs encephalon=6

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180

# The ways out of the yard are symbols on their lines, each named from the yard.
inspect symbols
expect-state symbols click observe "the way to Test Field" in "Test Yard" (way)
expect-state symbols click observe "Test Door" in "Test Yard" (way)
# The card keeps no way but its views: the yard has none, so the kind is not on it.
expect-no-state symbols click observe way in "Test Yard"

# What stands where nobody has been is shown and cannot be looked at yet: the wolf's den, two ways off.
expect-state symbols click observe hostile in "Test Den" x1 (disabled)
# Nor can a way neither of whose ends can be walked to.
expect-state symbols click observe "the way to Test Den" in "Test Wood" (way) (disabled)

# Under the pointer an unknown way says no more than that, on the clickable ground.
point observe "Test Field"
wait 1
expect-state pointer-label ground=yellow text=observe · an unknown way
point observe "Test Den"
wait 1
expect-state pointer-label text=a way · no known way there

# Observed, the way is the root of a tree hung from its line; the mind was asked for that way and no other.
strategy succeed
goal move
click observe "Test Field"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
expect-state trees element "the way to Test Field"
expect-no-state symbols click observe "the way to Test Field"
point think "Test Field"
wait 1
expect-state pointer-label text=think about the way to the test field

# Walked, the member stands at its other end, and the same tree is the way back to the yard: one
# way, seen from where the member stands.
click think "Test Field"
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
click act 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect-state where Test Field
expect-state trees element "the way to Test Yard"
expect-no-state trees element "the way to Test Field"

# The way out is a symbol like the rest.
point exit
wait 1
expect-state pointer-label ground=yellow text=LEAVE
quit
